nodecode-actvox is a rewrite of ActVox's ActVox/actvox-plugins:

  https://github.com/ActVox/actvox-plugins
  commit 76e394d381c3cf56632d7fd6c91d442c68b181f2
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 ActVox (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's inbox read, in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell
contract. The `actvox` CLI's `inbox --all --json` and `auth status --json`
are run and their JSON read, with the plugin's own rules for what counts as
waiting - an unacknowledged mention, or a task in an owner state with a next
action, a claimed task with a live lease being in progress - and its words for
each answer. The first-turn note is the :ROUND hook: one line, once a turn,
from a read the section caches. What was two MCP-side reads is here a tool
(`actvox_inbox`) and `/actvox inbox|status`.

Left out: the two prose skills (their guidance is the manual topic
`(help :actvox)` and the tool's own documentation), the `actvox` MCP server
itself - the CLI is the one path this cell reads through, so it needs no
OAuth sign-in of its own and no MCP connection - and the terminal setup and
`install-gate` commands. The cron wake gate is left out with them: its
`wakeAgent` line and its 15m/1h/6h backoff state file are how Hermes's cron
job skips an empty inbox, and Nodecode's cron cell schedules its own turns,
so the gate had nothing to gate. Nothing was added: no network call of the
cell's own, no credential, no write to ActVox.
